"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including the preoperative PSA of 7 and the pathological findings of Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3) with pT3b disease. Significant adverse features include extraprostatic extension, positive surgical margins, and seminal vesicle invasion. A notable countervailing finding is the absence of lymphovascular invasion. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy comparison shows a discrepancy, as the initial biopsy indicated Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) compared to the higher grade found post-surgery. Furthermore, no lymph nodes were removed, meaning nodal status assessment is unavailable and widens uncertainty regarding regional spread. Future prognosis would be significantly revised by postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory. The fixed estimated horizon is 42.09 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 25.25–58.93 months; its coverage has not been validated."
